{"type":"system","subtype":"background_tasks_changed","tasks":[{"task_id":"ba577izip","task_type":"local_bash","description":"cd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop; C=iter_1/candidate_5\ncat > $C/hypothesis.md << 'EOF'\nRefinement of `most_lopsided_stretch_aversion` (rank 3): people still find a sequence less random when one stretch of it shows a striking local heads/tails excess, and still judge it by their own ideal switching rate and sensitivity, personal weights on overall imbalance and the longest streak, shared weights on the final streak, mirror symmetry and run-length variety, and a personal guessing rate. The one change is that departures from one's ideal switching rate count differently in the two directions, and how lenient a person is toward switching more often than their ideal (relative to the cost of switching too rarely) is their own trait drawn from a population — some people barely mind over-alternation while others penalise it as much as streakiness — so people disagree about pairs of highly alternating sequences more than a single shared leniency (the incumbent's) allows.\nEOF\necho personal_over_alternation_leniency > $C/model_name.txt\npython3 - << 'EOF'\nsrc = open(\"models/asymmetric_tolerance_lopsided_stretch.py\").read()\ndoc_end = src.index('\"\"\"', 3) + 3\nnewdoc = '''\"\"\"Personal leniency toward over-alternation, on the most lopsided stretch model.\n\nRefinement of `most_lopsided_stretch_aversion`: one striking local heads/tails\nexcess still makes a sequence look designed, on top of the personal ideal\nswitching rate and sensitivity, personal weights on imbalance and the longest\nrun, shared weights on the final run, mirror symmetry and run-length variety,\nand a personal lapse rate. The one change: switching more often than one's\nideal costs a fraction of what the same shortfall costs, and that fraction is\neach person's own trait, drawn from a population.\n\"\"\"'''\nsrc = newdoc + src[doc_end:]\nold = '''    # Shared fraction of the ideal-rate penalty applied to over-alternation.\n    log_over = pm.Normal(\"log_over\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0)\n    over_frac = pm.Deterministic(\"over_frac\", pm.math.exp(log_over))\n'''\nnew = '''    # Personal fraction of the ideal-rate penalty applied to over-alternation\n    # (non-centred log-normal population).\n    mu_over = pm.Normal(\"mu_over\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0)\n    sigma_over = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_over\", sigma=0.7)\n    z_over = pm.Normal(\"z_over\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=MAX_PARTICIPANTS)\n    over_frac = pm.math.exp(mu_over + sigma_over * z_over)\n'''\nassert old in src\nsrc = src.replace(old, new)\nold2 = \"        return pt.sqr(dev) * pt.switch(dev > 0, over_frac, 1.0)\"\nassert old2 in src\nsrc = src.replace(old2, \"        return pt.sqr(dev) * pt.switch(dev > 0, over_frac[participant_id], 1.0)\")\nopen(\"iter_1/candidate_5/candidate.py\", \"w\").write(src)\nEOF\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run1/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/$C --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5"}],"uuid":"966f225d-59ab-4013-81f5-fab7a8abd44a","session_id":"ac2fa5a4-316d-46f5-a886-6f49876876a2"}
